<description>
Complete each partial copy of the yellow-marked 3x3 template by adding the template's yellow cells.

Input structure
- A black background contains scattered blue/teal distractors and one full 3x3 sprite whose yellow pixels mark the cells to add.
- The yellow pixels' bounding box is the full template window.
- Partial copies elsewhere already contain the template's non-yellow pixels in the same relative positions.

Rule
- Use the yellow bounding box as the 3x3 template.
- Search every 3x3 window for an exact match to the template's non-yellow pixels.
- At each matching window, paint yellow into the positions that are yellow in the template.

Key insight
- Yellow is not a target marker; it identifies the missing-cell mask to transfer onto every same-layout partial copy.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "yellow-marked 3x3 template sprite s",
  "dst": "3x3 grid windows d",
  "match_cond": "d matches s on every non-yellow cell and has bg/yellow at s.yellow-mask cells",
  "transform": "paint s.yellow-mask cells yellow in each matched d; leave all other pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 22x22, black background
  colors: black(0) background, blue(1) and azure(8) as support/distractor, yellow(4) as fill marker
  template:
    size: exactly 3x3, all 9 cells non-black
    composition: 3-5 support cells (blue/azure mix) + 4-6 yellow cells; both colors present in support
    yellow_bbox: equals the full 3x3 template (yellow cells define the fill mask)
  partial_copies:
    count: 1-2 copies placed elsewhere on the grid
    structure: support cells identical to template; yellow positions hold black (unfilled)
    no_overlap: 3x3 windows of template and all partials are non-overlapping
  distractors:
    colors: blue(1) and azure(8) only, scattered as mostly single pixels with occasional small clusters (1-7 cells)
    total_cells: 47-85 [observed]
    constraint: no 3x3 window in the grid (other than template/partials) may match the template support pattern
  output:
    same as input except each partial copy's black fill-mask cells become yellow

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Design a random 3x3 template with all cells non-black; assign 3-5 cells as support (blue/azure mix, at least one of each) and the rest as yellow
    2. Place the template on the 22x22 grid at a random position
    3. Place 1-2 partial copies (support cells identical, yellow positions filled with yellow) at non-overlapping positions -- these form the output state
    4. Scatter 47-85 distractor pixels (blue and azure) randomly on empty cells; after placement, verify no accidental 3x3 support-pattern matches exist (reject or remove offending pixels)
    5. Derive input by replacing yellow fill-mask cells in each partial copy with black (template itself keeps its yellow)
```
